{#
	Colour scheme control
	=====================
	A Light / Dark / System choice, used in the footer and on the Accessibility page. Import it like so:
	{% from "components/units/colour-scheme/colour-scheme.njk" import colourSchemeControl %}
	{{ colourSchemeControl("footer") }}

	- `idPrefix` keeps the `id`s and the radio group `name` unique when the control appears twice on one page.
	- Each radio button sits inside its `<label>`, so the whole option is one click / tap target. The label's `for`
	  still points at the radio's `id`, because some voice control software needs that link even when nested.
	- "System" follows the device setting. Its "(currently …)" text is two spans, and `_colour-scheme.scss`
	  hides the one that doesn't match the device setting, so it stays right without any JavaScript.
	- It's rendered `hidden`, because it can't work without JavaScript. `scripts/features/colourScheme.mjs`
	  shows it, ticks the current choice and saves changes. Without JavaScript the site simply follows the device.

	WHY NO INDENTATION / BLANK LINES IN THE MACRO'S OUTPUT? The Accessibility page is markdown, which is processed
	*after* Nunjucks. An indented line after a blank line becomes a code block, and a blank line ends an HTML block
	early. The `-` whitespace control (eg. `{%- ... %}`) keeps the output as one tight block of HTML.
#}

{% macro colourSchemeControl(idPrefix) -%}
<fieldset class="colour-scheme" hidden>
<legend class="colour-scheme__legend">Colour scheme</legend>
<span class="colour-scheme__options">
{%- for option in [
	{ value: "light", label: "Light" },
	{ value: "dark", label: "Dark" },
	{ value: "system", label: "System" }
] %}
<label class="colour-scheme__option" for="{{ idPrefix }}-colour-scheme-{{ option.value }}"><input type="radio" id="{{ idPrefix }}-colour-scheme-{{ option.value }}" name="{{ idPrefix }}-colour-scheme" value="{{ option.value }}"> <span>{{ option.label }}{% if option.value == "system" %} <span class="colour-scheme__current">(currently <span class="colour-scheme__if-light">light</span><span class="colour-scheme__if-dark">dark</span>)</span>{% endif %}</span></label>
{%- endfor %}
</span>
</fieldset>
{%- endmacro %}
